			],
			"Message": "chore(Project): Sync Element submodule with event payload fixes and webview bridge\n\nSubmodule synchronization bringing critical fixes and a new feature:\n\n1. Mountain - Event Payload Alignment:\n   - Fix event channel names: terminal `opened`→`create`, `closed`→`exit`, debug `stop`→`sessionEnd`, statusbar `create`→`set-entry`, webview `message`→`post-message`, progress→`notification/progress-update`\n   - Correct payload keys to camelCase for OutputProvider, StatusBarProvider, TreeViewProvider, UserInterfaceProvider, Window\n   - Add parameter key fallback: probe camelCase first then snake_case for backward compat\n   - Fix SCM RootUri: reconstruct full URI from scheme/authority/path instead of relative URLs\n   - Add command registry emissions for Sky's workbench command palette\n\n2. Sky - New Webview Post-Message Bridge:\n   - Add handler for `sky://webview/post-message` to dispatch `cel:webview:post-message` events to renderer\n   - Bridges extension `postMessage` path from Cocoon with `{handle, message}` shape distinct from workbench-RPC `{panelId, method, params}`\n\n3. Dependencies:\n   - Cocoon, Echo, Rest: pozil/auto-assign-issue 2.2.0→3.0.0\n   - Echo: @cloudflare/workers-types, miniflare, wrangler updates\n\n4. Common: Document deprecated aliases UIShowInputBoxRequest and UIShowQuickPickRequest\n\nImpact: Terminal panes, tree views, status bar entries, and command palette entries now render correctly. Extensions can communicate back to Sky UI via the new webview post-message bridge.",
			"SHA": "ebf8546260e42a5029b846b7d74edb1ce8323180"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-26T22:47:09Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				102,
				1
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Project): Standardize DTO serialization to camelCase and fix SCM provider registration\n\nSubmodule synchronization across Mountain, Mist, and Rest:\n\n1. Mountain: Migrate DTO serialization from PascalCase to camelCase across 13 files (CustomDocumentStateDTO, DocumentStateDTO, MarkerDataDTO, etc.) to match the wire format expected by Wind/Sky.\n\n2. Mountain: Fix SCM provider registration - change PascalCase keys (\"ID\", \"Label\", \"RootUri\") to camelCase (\"id\", \"label\", \"rootUri\") in RegisterScmProvider and add missing \"providerHandle\" field in RegisterScmResourceGroup.\n\n3. Mountain: Add #[allow(dead_code)] to 15 structs used only in specific build configs and set MACOSX_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET=10.13 for broader compatibility.\n\n4. Mist: Add #![allow(non_snake_case)] lint to permit PascalCase naming conventions consistent with CodeEditorLand standards.\n\n5. Rest: Switch binary entry point from Library.rs to Main.rs with proper async tokio runtime.\n\nImpact: Wind/Sky now receive correctly formatted DTOs with camelCase keys, SCM source control providers properly register, and the Rest bundler has correct binary structure.",
			"SHA": "9203102a8778770cf3de193abaec23edf1e83491"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-26T20:30:42Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				102,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Add workspace trust handlers for vscode.git and mute API gap logs\n\nSubmodule synchronization bringing two Mountain changes:\n\n1. Workspace Trust Handlers:\n   - Implement Workspace.RequestResourceTrust and Workspace.IsResourceTrusted handlers\n   - Route through Mountain instead of falling back to Cocoon's permissive heuristic\n   - vscode.git's Model.openRepository now calls these before constructing Repository\n   - Enables GenerateRouteManifest.sh to auto-switch Cocoon from heuristic to gRPC routing\n   - Future work can replace trust-by-default with real per-OS trust queries (Gatekeeper/SmartScreen/xattrs)\n\n2. Log Noise Reduction:\n   - Mute vscode-api-gap dev logs in short mode\n   - These log when extensions use unshimmed vscode API methods\n   - Useful for API gap audits but noisy in default dev runs\n   - Enable via LAND_DEV_LOG=all or LAND_DEV_LOG=vscode-api-gap when needed\n\nImpact: vscode.git extension now properly routes through Mountain's trust handlers with future extensibility for real OS-level trust queries.",
			"SHA": "bd777531a7bf4fdfeb693820ba44cc9efc7237b6"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-26T20:10:59Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				102,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Project): Sync Element submodule with bug fixes and URI improvements\n\nSubmodule synchronization bringing in latest changes addressing search and URI handling:\n\n1. Sky: Fix text search result mapping to use Mountain's actual response format - `Hit.resource` instead of `Hit.uri`, and `Hit.matches[]` array with `preview` and `line_number` instead of flat hit shape. Add backwards-compat support for old flat `{uri, lineNumber, preview}` format.\n\n2. Sky: Fix search:findFiles IPC call to include required null exclude parameter. Previously MaxResults was shifted into wrong slot, causing glob extractor to ignore max and default to 10000. This resolves empty search results.\n\n3. Output: Add missing URI class import to ExposeWorkbenchAccessor transform, enabling SkyBridge to construct resource objects the workbench accepts directly.\n\n4. Mountain: Use DebugOnce instead of dev_log! for unregistered view-action and workbench-internal commands to reduce log noise.\n\nImpact: Text search and file search now return correct results using Mountain's response format, eliminating empty results from parameter order mismatch.",
			"SHA": "efc8c47b9443c033122f0f4d22e4086edb1c693f"
		}
	],
